  "notes": "CompCert verified C compiler (https://compcert.org). Proof assistant: Coq (rebranded as Rocq ~2024; both names appear in commit messages). Main proof dirs: backend/, cfrontend/, common/, lib/, aarch64/, arm/, x86/, x86_32/, x86_64/, powerpc/, riscV/. Vendored libs excluded: flocq/ (floating-point library), MenhirLib/ (parser lib). Build: 'make proof' compiles all .v to .vo. Makefile 'check-admitted' target greps for admit|Admitted|ADMITTED (confirms all three as hole markers). GitHub PRs merged as 'Merge pull request #NNN from AbsInt/branch'. Bug refs use 'bug NNNNN' format. .vp files are CompCert-specific preprocessed Coq files, converted to .v via tools/ndfun; they contain Nondetfunction declarations for architecture-specific SelectOp, ConstpropOp, SelectLong. CompCert-specific Ltac tactics: monadInv (inversion on 'res' monad values), exploit (forward reasoning by instantiating universally quantified hypotheses), extlia (extended lia for pointer arithmetic with Ptrofs). ia32/ directory reorganized into x86_32/ and x86_64/ in commit 88334171 (~2016). Hole markers are extremely rare in current codebase (0 in HEAD); all challenges come from development-era history (pre-2017). Proof style is tactic mode with heavy Ltac automation (EvalOp, InvEval, TrivialExists, Simpl, DeclHelper, UseHelper macros). Commit subjects often include module name prefix: 'ModuleName: description'. Most proof work is classified as proof_add since CompCert rarely leaves admitted gaps.",
